<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Estimating Measure by reading single Decrement Tables(Life Tables)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Use the BRAZIL \(1950\) LIFETABLE given below to answer the question that follows.
</p>
 <a href="https://drive.google.com/uc?export=download&id=1NfHh5bPWXGnfTfxSl68Ie5wy2umo3HQ8">Download Brazillian Demography Life tables</a>
<br>
<br>
<p>Using the life tables for Brazil, estimate the following measures.</p>
<ol class="HELM_parts">
<li> In \(1946\), there were \({@population@}\) female births, estimate the number of girls aged last birthday on \(31-12-{@1946+years@}\).</li>
<p>Estimate number of girls aged last birthday on \(31-12-{@1946+years@} = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<br>
<li> A couple aged (both) \(25\) years have male twins. What is the probability that one parent or both will die before either of the sons in the next \({@event_a_b@}\) years.</li>
<p>(Note: leave you answer to \(3 \text{dp}\).)</p>
 </ol>
<p><b>i.</b>  Probability that the male parent will die before either of the son \(=\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]][[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p><b>ii.</b>  Probability that the female parent will die before either of the son \(=\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]][[feedback:prt3]]</p>
<p><b>iii.</b>  Probability that the both parents will die before either of the son \(=\) [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]][[feedback:prt4]]</p>
<p><b>iv.</b>  Probability that the sons will die before the \({@event_a_b@}\) years. \(=\) [[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]][[feedback:prt5]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<ol class="HELM_parts">
<li>  Let the number of population over the years \({@1946+years@} -1946={@years@}\) be denoted as \(l_{@years@}\) and the original population be \(l_0\)</li>
<p>Thus,Estimate number of girls aged last birthday on \(31-12-{@1946+years@} \) is;</p>
<p>
\(\begin{align}
\text{Estimate number} &= \displaystyle \frac{l_{@years@}}{l_0} \times {@population@}\\
&=\displaystyle \frac{{@l_x@}} {{@l_0@}} \times {@population@}\\
&={@sol1@}\\
\end{align}\)
</p>
<br>
<li></li>
 </ol>
<p><b>i.</b>  Probability that the male parent will die before either of the son.</p>
<p>Let \(A\) be the event that the man die before the next {@event_a_b@} years and </p>
<p>\(l^m_{@25+event_a_b@}\) be population of men in \({@event_a_b@}\) and \(l_{25}\) be the population of men at \(25\) years.</p>
<p>\( \begin{align}
P(A)&=1-\displaystyle \frac{l^m_{@25+event_a_b@}}{l_{25}}\\
&=1-\displaystyle \frac{{@l_m_x@}}{{@l_m_age@}}\\
&=1-{@decimalplaces(soln2,3)@}\\
&={@ta3@}\\
\end{align}\)</p>
<br>
<p><b>ii.</b>  Probability that the female parent will die before either of the son. </p>
<p>Let \(B\) be the event that the female die before the next {@event_a_b@} years and </p>
<p>\(l^f_{@25+event_a_b@}\) be population of females in \({@event_a_b@}\) and \(l_{25}\) be the population of female at \(25\) years.</p>
<p>\( \begin{align}
P(A)&=1-\displaystyle \frac{l^f_{@25+event_a_b@}}{l_{25}}\\
&=1-\displaystyle \frac{{@l_f_x@}}{{@l_f_age@}}\\
&=1-{@decimalplaces(soln1,3)@}\\
&={@ta2@}\\
\end{align}\)</p>
<br>
<p><b>iii.</b>  Probability that the both parents will die before either of the son.</p>
<p>Probability that either or both parents die before the next {@event_a_b@} years.</p>
<p>\(P(A \cup B)=P(A)+P(B)-P(A)P(B)\)</p>
<p>\(\begin{align}
P(A \cup B)&={@ta3@}+{@ta2@}-({@ta2@} \times{@ta3@})\\
&={@ta4@}\\
\end{align}\)</p>
<br>
<p><b>iv.</b> Probability that the sons will die before the \({@event_a_b@}\) years.</p>
<p>Let \(C_1\) and \(C_2\) be the events that the sons will die before the \({@event_a_b@}\) years.</p>
<p>\(P(C_1)=1-\displaystyle \frac{l_{@event_a_b@}}{l_0}\) which is \(=P(C_2)=1-\displaystyle \frac{l_{@event_a_b@}}{l_0}\)</p>
<p>\(\begin{align}
P(C_1)&=P(C_2)\\
&=1-\displaystyle \frac{{@l_x_sons@}}{100000}\\
&={@s1@}\\
&=2({@s1@})-({@s1@}^2)\\
&={@ta5@}
\end{align}\)</p>
<p></p>]]></text>
